// Source: a Cpp1 loop and pointer example (`++i`, `&x`, `*p`) ported
// literally. common.md: `++`, `&` and `*` are postfix in Cpp2.
// expect-error: prefix '++var' is not valid Cpp2; use postfix 'var++' instead
// expect-error: prefix '&var' address-of is not valid Cpp2; use postfix 'var&' instead
main: () = {
    i := 0;
    ++i;
    p := &i;
    std::cout << p* << "\n";
}
